    },
    "content": {
      "rendered": "\n<div class=\"wp-block-media-text alignwide has-media-on-the-right is-stacked-on-mobile is-vertically-aligned-center has-secondary-background-color has-background\"><div class=\"wp-block-media-text__content\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-group is-vertical is-layout-flex wp-container-core-group-is-layout-ce03cda6 wp-block-group-is-layout-flex\" style=\"padding-top:2em;padding-right:2em;padding-bottom:2em;padding-left:2em\">\n<p class=\"has-foreground-color has-text-color wp-block-paragraph\" style=\"font-size:36px;line-height:1.2\"><strong>Solar Power Water Pump</strong></p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-body-text-color has-text-color has-extra-small-font-size wp-block-paragraph\">&#8220;A solar-powered water pump harnesses energy from the sun to efficiently pump water without relying on grid electricity. Its advantages include cost-effectiveness, eco-friendliness, reliability in remote areas, low operational costs, and suitability for various applications like irrigation, drinking water supply, livestock watering, and pond maintenance.&#8221;</p>\n</div>\n</div><figure class=\"wp-block-media-text__media\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"800\" height=\"554\" src=\"https://srhsolar.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/Solar-Pump-Technologies.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-146 size-full\" srcset=\"https://srhsolar.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/Solar-Pump-Technologies.png 800w, https://srhsolar.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/Solar-Pump-Technologies-300x208.png 300w, https://srhsolar.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/Solar-Pump-Technologies-768x532.png 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 800px) 100vw, 800px\" /></figure></div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-media-text alignwide is-stacked-on-mobile is-vertically-aligned-center has-secondary-background-color has-background\"><figure class=\"wp-block-media-text__media\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"850\" height=\"619\" src=\"https://srhsolar.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/Off-grid-PV-System-Schematic.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-144 size-full\" srcset=\"https://srhsolar.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/Off-grid-PV-System-Schematic.png 850w, https://srhsolar.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/Off-grid-PV-System-Schematic-300x218.png 300w, https://srhsolar.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/Off-grid-PV-System-Schematic-768x559.png 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 850px) 100vw, 850px\" /></figure><div class=\"wp-block-media-text__content\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-group is-layout-flow wp-block-group-is-layout-flow\" style=\"padding-top:2em;padding-right:2em;padding-bottom:2em;padding-left:2em\">\n<p class=\"has-foreground-color has-text-color wp-block-paragraph\" style=\"font-size:36px;line-height:1.2\">Off Grid Photovoltaic System</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-body-text-color has-text-color has-extra-small-font-size wp-block-paragraph\">&#8220;An off-grid PV (photovoltaic) system is a standalone solar power setup that operates independently from the main electrical grid. It comprises solar panels, batteries for energy storage, charge controllers, and inverters. Advantages include complete energy self-sufficiency, especially in remote locations or areas with unreliable grid access. Off-grid PV systems offer clean, renewable energy, reducing dependence on traditional power sources, lowering electricity bills, and providing electricity where grid connections are not feasible or too costly.&#8221;</p>\n</div>\n</div></div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-media-text alignwide has-media-on-the-right is-stacked-on-mobile is-vertically-aligned-center has-secondary-background-color has-background\"><div class=\"wp-block-media-text__content\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-group is-layout-flow wp-block-group-is-layout-flow\" style=\"padding-top:2em;padding-right:2em;padding-bottom:2em;padding-left:2em\">\n<p class=\"has-foreground-color has-text-color wp-block-paragraph\" style=\"font-size:36px;line-height:1.2\">On Grid Solar System</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-extra-small-font-size wp-block-paragraph\">&#8220;An on-grid solar system, also known as a grid-tied or grid-connected system, works in tandem with the main electrical grid. It consists of solar panels, inverters, and a connection to the grid. This setup allows excess solar energy to be exported to the grid and provides electricity from the grid when solar production is insufficient. Advantages include the ability to sell excess power back to the grid (net metering), reduced electricity bills, lower environmental impact by using clean energy, and the reliability of grid backup during low solar production periods or high energy demand.&#8221;</p>\n</div>\n</div><figure class=\"wp-block-media-text__media\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"500\" height=\"500\" src=\"https://srhsolar.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/on-grid-solar-system.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-142 size-full\" srcset=\"https://srhsolar.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/on-grid-solar-system.jpg 500w, https://srhsolar.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/on-grid-solar-system-300x300.jpg 300w, https://srhsolar.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/on-grid-solar-system-150x150.jpg 150w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 500px) 100vw, 500px\" /></figure></div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-media-text alignwide is-stacked-on-mobile is-vertically-aligned-center has-secondary-background-color has-background\"><figure class=\"wp-block-media-text__media\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"850\" height=\"507\" src=\"https://srhsolar.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/Grid-connected-PV-system.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-147 size-full\" srcset=\"https://srhsolar.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/Grid-connected-PV-system.png 850w, https://srhsolar.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/Grid-connected-PV-system-300x179.png 300w, https://srhsolar.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/Grid-connected-PV-system-768x458.png 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 850px) 100vw, 850px\" /></figure><div class=\"wp-block-media-text__content\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-group is-layout-flow wp-block-group-is-layout-flow\" style=\"padding-top:2em;padding-right:2em;padding-bottom:2em;padding-left:2em\">\n<p class=\"has-foreground-color has-text-color wp-block-paragraph\" style=\"font-size:36px;line-height:1.2\">Grid Connected Photovoltaic System</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-extra-small-font-size wp-block-paragraph\">&#8220;A grid-connected PV (photovoltaic) system is directly linked to the main electrical grid. It comprises solar panels, inverters, and connection points to the grid infrastructure. Advantages include the ability to supply excess electricity back to the grid, lowering electricity bills through net metering, reduced environmental impact by using clean energy, reliability with grid-supplied power during low solar production, and the potential to earn incentives or credits for surplus energy supplied to the grid. These systems offer an efficient way to generate renewable energy while remaining connected to the established power grid for added reliability and flexibility.&#8221;</p>\n</div>\n</div></div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-media-text alignwide has-media-on-the-right is-stacked-on-mobile is-vertically-aligned-center has-secondary-background-color has-background\"><div class=\"wp-block-media-text__content\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-group is-layout-flow wp-block-group-is-layout-flow\" style=\"padding-top:2em;padding-right:2em;padding-bottom:2em;padding-left:2em\">\n<p class=\"has-foreground-color has-text-color wp-block-paragraph\" style=\"font-size:36px;line-height:1.2\">Solar-powered street lights</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-extra-small-font-size wp-block-paragraph\">&#8220;Solar-powered street lights utilize solar panels to generate and store energy during the day, powering LED lights for illumination at night. Advantages include cost savings from reduced electricity bills, eco-friendliness by using renewable energy, easy installation without the need for extensive wiring, low maintenance, and reliability, especially in areas with limited access to the power grid. These lights contribute to sustainable and efficient urban lighting solutions, offering increased safety and visibility while reducing overall energy consumption and environmental impact.&#8221;</p>\n</div>\n</div><figure class=\"wp-block-media-text__media\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"800\" height=\"554\" src=\"https://srhsolar.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/02/streetpixa.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-181 size-full\" srcset=\"https://srhsolar.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/02/streetpixa.png 800w, https://srhsolar.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/02/streetpixa-300x208.png 300w, https://srhsolar.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/02/streetpixa-768x532.png 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 800px) 100vw, 800px\" /></figure></div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-media-text alignwide is-stacked-on-mobile is-vertically-aligned-center has-secondary-background-color has-background\"><figure class=\"wp-block-media-text__media\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1001\" height=\"1001\" src=\"https://srhsolar.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/product2.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-64 size-full\" srcset=\"https://srhsolar.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/product2.jpg 1001w, https://srhsolar.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/product2-300x300.jpg 300w, https://srhsolar.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/product2-150x150.jpg 150w, https://srhsolar.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/product2-768x768.jpg 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1001px) 100vw, 1001px\" /></figure><div class=\"wp-block-media-text__content\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-group is-layout-flow wp-block-group-is-layout-flow\" style=\"padding-top:2em;padding-right:2em;padding-bottom:2em;padding-left:2em\">\n<p class=\"has-foreground-color has-text-color wp-block-paragraph\" style=\"font-size:36px;line-height:1.2\">The Smart Home Solution</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-extra-small-font-size wp-block-paragraph\">&#8220;A smart home solution powered by solar energy integrates solar panels with advanced technology to create an energy-efficient, connected living environment. This setup combines solar power generation with smart devices and automation for increased energy management and convenience. Advantages include reduced energy costs through solar generation, smart energy monitoring and control, integration with smart appliances and devices, enhanced sustainability, and the ability to remotely manage and optimize energy usage, leading to a more eco-friendly and cost-effective home.&#8221;</p>\n</div>\n</div></div>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-text-align-center has-primary-color has-text-color has-product-heading-font-size wp-block-paragraph\">Get A Quote</p>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-contact-form-7-contact-form-selector\"><div role=\"form\" class=\"wpcf7\" id=\"wpcf7-f199-o1\" lang=\"en-US\" dir=\"ltr\">\n<div class=\"screen-reader-response\"><p role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\" aria-atomic=\"true\"></p> <ul></ul></div>\n<form action=\"/wp-json/wp/v2/pages?per_page=100#wpcf7-f199-o1\" method=\"post\" class=\"wpcf7-form init\" novalidate=\"novalidate\" data-status=\"init\">\n<div style=\"display: none;\">\n<input type=\"hidden\" name=\"_wpcf7\" value=\"199\" />\n<input type=\"hidden\" name=\"_wpcf7_version\" value=\"5.4.1\" />\n<input type=\"hidden\" name=\"_wpcf7_locale\" value=\"en_US\" />\n<input type=\"hidden\" name=\"_wpcf7_unit_tag\" value=\"wpcf7-f199-o1\" />\n<input type=\"hidden\" name=\"_wpcf7_container_post\" value=\"0\" />\n<input type=\"hidden\" name=\"_wpcf7_posted_data_hash\" value=\"\" />\n<input type=\"hidden\" name=\"_wpcf7_recaptcha_response\" value=\"\" />\n</div>\n<div class=\"form-group\">\n    <span class=\"wpcf7-form-control-wrap user-name\"><input type=\"text\" name=\"user-name\" value=\"\" size=\"40\" class=\"wpcf7-form-control wpcf7-text wpcf7-validates-as-required form-control\" aria-required=\"true\" aria-invalid=\"false\" placeholder=\"Name *\" /></span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"form-group\">\n    <span class=\"wp